// A solution file (as the frontend's): it checks nothing itself and names the two
// projects, so an editor opens each file in the project that holds it, a test with the
// tests' settings rather than in a project of its own it would infer.
// - tsconfig.build.json: the source (src/, without the tests), with noUncheckedIndexedAccess
//   on; what `npm run build` and the production image compile.
// - tsconfig.test.json: the tests and their helpers (src/**/__tests__, *.test.ts, src/test),
//   with that flag off.
// `npm run type-check` checks both; a bare `tsc --noEmit` here checks nothing (name a project
// with -p, as the script does).
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.build.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.test.json" }
  ]
}
